<decision #track.add-eidolon-natural-language-workflow-authoring.actor-boundary { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" }
(
  <question ?>Who owns semantic generation and who owns resource writes?</?>
  <answer { } (
    <raw-answer ?>Eidolon actor generates; WorkflowComponent validates and writes.</?>
    <decision-text ?>The coordinator delegates semantic authoring to an Eidolon child actor, which may mutate resources only through native workflow tools.</?>
    <rationale ?>This prevents both a deterministic heuristic pretending to be AI authoring and an actor bypassing resource authority.</?>
  )>
)>

<decision #track.add-eidolon-natural-language-workflow-authoring.cli-runtime { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" }
(
  <question ?>How does the workflow CLI obtain AI generation?</?>
  <answer { } (
    <raw-answer ?>Invoke the in-process Eidolon headless runtime.</?>
    <decision-text ?>CLI create/edit runs an Eidolon turn that routes to WorkflowAuthor; it never spawns an external agent executable.</?>
    <rationale ?>Eidolon already is the AI runtime and should remain the only provider/session authority.</?>
  )>
)>
